{"chunk_id": "ae19f0a3b5d6", "text": "Dhritarashtra asks Sanjaya what happened after Bhishma\u2019s terrible vow on the battlefield. Sanjaya describes a catastrophic phase of the Kurukshetra war: Bhishma charges the Pandava forces and devastates their army with overwhelming skill, appearing everywhere at once as his arrows slaughter warriors, elephants, and horses. The battlefield becomes a grotesque landscape of severed limbs and rivers of blood, and the Pandava troops begin to rout even in the presence of Krishna and Arjuna. Urged by Krishna, Arjuna finally confronts his grandsire. Their duel is fierce; Arjuna repeatedly cuts Bhishma\u2019s bows while Bhishma praises his prowess. Seeing Arjuna still restrained by respect, Krishna\u2014unable to bear the carnage\u2014leaps from the chariot with his Sudarshana discus to kill Bhishma himself, breaking his vow not to fight, but Arjuna stops him and promises to fight with full resolve, after which the battle surges again.\nBhishma devastates the Pandava army until Krishna, enraged, nearly breaks his vow to attack him, before Arjuna rallies and counterattacks with celestial weapons.\nThemes: divine restraint, battle fury, duty vs reverence, Krishna and Arjuna partnership, apocalyptic warfare", "vector": [-0.00046323167043738067, -0.019562045112252235, 0.002185373567044735, 0.026960251852869987, -0.011630574241280556, 0.027648771181702614, -0.013338372111320496, -0.00833648256957531, -0.014283398166298866, -0.02150609903037548, 0.01629495434463024, 0.018549516797065735, -0.0010226535378023982, -0.00035797091550193727, 0.014094392769038677, 0.006611809600144625, 0.04825034737586975, 0.0034071574918925762, 0.02539420872926712, -0.024260176345705986, -0.01168457604944706, 0.0005265146610327065, 0.001094374223612249, 0.02282913587987423, -0.017334483563899994, 0.04071713611483574, 0.0012951923999935389, -0.019454043358564377, 0.0014369463315233588, -0.005649907514452934, -0.010665297508239746, 0.005670158192515373, 0.0007285